    "done_when": "At the committed head: (1) a test in tests/test_budget_window_length.py builds a codex-sub group whose recorded seven-day receipt is stale (observed 2026-09-26, reset passed) while its members' account-surface reading is fresh (10,080-minute primary window, 3% used, 0.84% elapsed), and asserts that the group allowance, the bar and the dispatch pace record all read the account-surface figure, not the receipt; it fails at base f8cb9464d and passes at head. (2) A test asserts that at that reading, with pace_multiple 1.1, a new implement-role codex dispatch is held by the group pace with a reason naming utilisation, allowance and reset time, while a review-role dispatch is admitted. (3) A test asserts that a reported window of 1,440 minutes is retained and paced by its own elapsed fraction rather than dropped. (4) The existing week test is changed so it fails when the derivation is fixed at 43,200 minutes, shown in a recorded log. (5) The command /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/reckon crew preflight --project reckon --role implement, run from the worktree with PYTHONPATH set to it, prints the codex-sub group with source account-surface and its live utilisation, allowance and held verdict; that output is quoted in docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/codex-pacing-live.html. The gate is tests/test_budget_window_length.py, tests/test_budget.py, tests/test_reserve.py, tests/test_pace.py and tests/test_preflight_pace.py before and after, with zero added failure ids (test_one_stamp_reader_dates_a_record_for_both_surfaces fails at base already).",
